---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy — 100% Client-Side Privacy Guarantee | WordCountr Pro";
const pageDescription = "WordCountr Pro Privacy Policy. Learn how our 100% client-side architecture guarantees your writing, documents, and manuscripts never leave your device.";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  canonicalSlug="privacy"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
    
    <!-- Top Pill & Title -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="mono-eyebrow inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-[#0070f3]/25 bg-[#0070f3]/10 px-3 py-1 text-[#0070f3] mb-4">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#0070f3]"></span>
        <span>Zero-Data Transmission Architecture</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed]">
        Privacy Policy &amp; Data Guarantee
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-[#8f8f8f] leading-relaxed">
        Effective Date: November 2026 · Built on the principle that your private thoughts, confidential manuscripts, and academic drafts should never touch a remote server.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Guarantee Box -->
    <div class="rounded-[10px] border border-[#0070f3]/30 bg-[#0070f3]/5 dark:bg-[#0070f3]/10 p-6 sm:p-8 mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0070f3] mb-2 tracking-tight">The Foundational Guarantee: 100% Local Execution</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] leading-relaxed">
        Every metric computed by WordCountr Pro — including word counts, character totals, reading durations, Flesch-Kincaid readability scores, keyword density analyses, and file parsing — executes <strong>entirely inside your browser's local JavaScript runtime</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-[#0070f3] font-medium">
        Zero text packets transmitted · Zero cloud databases · Zero server logs
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Detailed Policy Sections -->
    <div class="vercel-card p-6 sm:p-10 space-y-8 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] dark:text-[#a1a1a1] leading-relaxed">
      
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">1. Information We Do Not Collect</h3>
        <p class="mb-2">
          Unlike traditional web-based text tools, WordCountr Pro is architecturally incapable of storing or intercepting your content. We do not collect, store, transmit, or process:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-[#666666] dark:text-[#8f8f8f]">
          <li>Any text, articles, essays, manuscripts, or notes pasted or typed into the workspace.</li>
          <li>Any uploaded documents, including PDF files (.pdf), Word documents (.docx), Markdown files (.md), or plain text files (.txt).</li>
          <li>Personally Identifiable Information (PII) such as your name, email address, physical address, or phone number.</li>
          <li>Keystroke logging or typing cadence patterns.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">2. No AI Training or Model Fine-Tuning</h3>
        <p>
          Many popular online writing utilities, spell-checkers, and counters secretly harvest user submissions to train commercial generative AI and large language models (LLMs). <strong>WordCountr Pro does not participate in AI training.</strong> Because your data never leaves your device's memory, it is mathematically and technically impossible for our team, hosting providers, or third-party AI labs to scrape or ingest your creative or confidential work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">3. Document Parsing in Local Browser Memory</h3>
        <p>
          When you drag and drop a Microsoft Word (.docx) or PDF document into WordCountr Pro, the binary file is read directly into your device's RAM using client-side WebAssembly and JavaScript libraries (<a href="https://mozilla.github.io/pdf.js/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline">PDF.js</a> and <a href="https://github.com/mwilliamson/mammoth.js" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline">Mammoth.js</a>). The file is parsed into text without triggering a single HTTP POST request.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">4. LocalStorage &amp; Session Auto-Recovery</h3>
        <p>
          To prevent accidental work loss from accidental browser refreshes, battery failures, or tab closures, WordCountr Pro automatically writes your current editor buffer to your browser's native <code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>wordcountr-draft</code>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This data remains solely inside your browser's local sandbox on your physical device. It is never synchronized across devices and never uploaded to any cloud. You can permanently erase your stored draft at any time by clicking the <strong>Clear</strong> button in the workspace toolbar.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">5. Cookies and Web Trackers</h3>
        <p>
          WordCountr Pro does not use tracking cookies, advertising beacons, fingerprinting scripts, or cross-site behavioral tracking. The only data saved in client storage are your functional preferences (e.g., your selected light/dark theme preference in <code>wordcountr-theme</code> and your optional draft text).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">6. Third-Party Infrastructure</h3>
        <p>
          Static assets (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, WebAssembly bundles, and Google Fonts) are served via GitHub Pages and global Content Delivery Networks (CDNs). These providers may log standard HTTP request metadata (such as IP addresses and user-agent strings) for security, DDoS mitigation, and server health. None of these logs contain or correlate with your workspace text.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">7. GDPR and CCPA Compliance</h3>
        <p>
          Because WordCountr Pro does not collect, process, or sell personal data, we inherently fulfill the requirements of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), and international privacy frameworks:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-[#666666] dark:text-[#8f8f8f] mt-2">
          <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> Erasing your browser cookies or clicking "Clear" immediately purges all trace of your work.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Portability:</strong> Your work can be exported instantly to .txt, Markdown, or clipboard at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>No Sale of Data:</strong> We do not sell, rent, or monetize user data under any circumstances.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#171717] dark:text-[#ededed] mb-2 tracking-tight">8. Contact &amp; Questions</h3>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding our privacy architecture or security model, please contact our maintainers at <a href="mailto:hello@wordcountr.app" class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline font-mono">hello@wordcountr.app</a> or visit our <a href={`${base}/contact`} class="text-[#0070f3] hover:underline">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Return to Workspace Button -->
    <div class="mt-8 text-center sm:text-left">
      <a href={`${base}/`} class="vercel-btn-primary inline-flex">
        <span>← Back to Word Counter Workspace</span>
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
